                <pb facs="0846" n="760" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg760"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-06"><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Leishman reports that he has received two notes from the Sublime Porte, one
                    with reference to American consular protection of Cuban citizens, and the other
                    with reference to the insurance question. He has notified the Sublime Porte that
                    unless the schools and other matters are settled within the next few days he
                    will feel compelled to press the Beirut matter, intimating at the same time that
                    if all other pending questions are satisfactorily settled, he will endeavor to
                    smooth over the Beirut trouble.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
